# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the ASAN CI (.github/workflows/hipblaslt-asan-ci.yml).
#
# These suppress *only* the ROCm HSA runtime's process-teardown leaks — signal,
# queue, and KFD event objects that libhsa-runtime64.so allocates once and never
# frees at exit. They are runtime internals, not defects in any BLAS library, and
# every BLAS/SOLVER test binary reports the identical set (~5784 bytes / 101 allocs
# rooted in rocr::AMD::hsa_amd_signal_create / AqlQueue / hsaKmtCreateEventCtx).
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: a leak whose stack does NOT pass through one of
# these frames (e.g. an actual leak in rocBLAS/rocSOLVER/hipSOLVER/hipBLAS/hipBLASLt)
# is NOT suppressed and still fails the job. This keeps leak detection ON without
# red-flagging the unactionable runtime teardown noise.
leak:rocr::AMD::
leak:hsaKmt
leak:libhsa-runtime64.so
